  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "While holding a QvPen in hand and holding the Tab key to draw in place in desktop mode, the mouse cursor highlights prints which means the Quick Menu prints UI disruptively in Build `1918` and later (Build `1921`) where in Build `1902` and earlier it did not. See the attached videos for comparison.\n\nSteps to reproduce:\n\n1. Launch VRChat in desktop mode.\n\n2. Print something (a \"bingo card\") with VRC+ in a world with a QvPen.\n\n3. Grab a QvPen from the world.\n\n4. Go near the print and while standing in place, start drawing on the print with a QvPen while holding the Tab key.\n\n5. Compare behavior to previous and current live builds (or watch the attached videos).\n\nExpected result: When holding an object like a QvPen in hand (which stays in hand without holding the left mouse button), holding the Tab key should not highlight prints. This behavior is correct in Build `1902`.\n\nActual result: In build `1918` and later (Build `1921`), the print details UI keeps popping up disruptively while drawing on a print when a QvPen is held in hand while the Tab key is held.\n\nTested with Build `1902` and Build `1921`. (Please note, the drawings on video are for show/testing. Don't read into them too much.)",
